  cal-20261002-s4-051,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would one specific hand-calculation question posted now get answers faster than the parked forum post in November?,"The post is parked until 1 November. Source: my notes, 2 October.",post one question now,keep it parked,notes,68,64,72,82,74,exploit,Resolved true if a note by 2026-10-31 records answers to a question posted in October; false otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-052,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would writing the Calibrator blog post myself teach me more than editing a crewmate's draft?,"The post is due 31 October, starting from a crewmate's draft. Source: my notes, 2 October.",write it myself,start from a crewmate's draft,notes,66,64,74,76,76,exploit,"Resolved by the published post's note: true if I wrote it from scratch and the note credits that with something learned.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-053,cal-2026-10-02-s4,"Would showing how a past answer resolved, on a later card, change my answer on that card?","Earlier credences are now left out of context lines; outcomes are not. Source: my notes, 2 October.",quote resolved outcomes in later context lines,keep outcomes in raw.toon only,calibration,76,60,84,60,78,explore,Resolved by comparing re-asks with and without a quoted outcome once ten of each exist; unresolved until then.,2027-03-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-054,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Is restoring garbled text from the published session file costing more than ten minutes per recording?,"All three pasted exports arrived garbled; the published sessions are clean. Source: site commit 5f17cd4.",fix the garbling at its source this week,keep restoring from the published file,project,70,72,74,60,80,exploit,"Resolved by a later recording note on time spent: true if restoring took more than ten minutes; unresolved otherwise.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-055,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Should the next crewmate go to structural tools rather than to mathematics?,"The next crewmate goes to mathematics or structural tools. Source: my notes, 2 October.",brief a structural tool next,brief a mathematics visual next,notes,70,76,70,58,82,exploit,"Resolved by the next crewmate task in either area: true if it is a structural tool.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-056,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Will the ten cards I would least like to answer in this session draw more of my answers between 35 and 65 than the rest?,"Each session so far had one or two answers between 35 and 65. Source: raw.toon.",keep ten uncomfortable cards in every session,drop them,calibration,72,60,80,64,80,exploit,"Resolved from this session's export: true if the share of answers between 35 and 65 is higher on the uncomfortable cards (001, 002, 004, 008, 011, 016, 018, 020, 024, 029) than on the rest.",next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-057,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Will I test one of my site's WebMCP tools from ChatGPT Desktop by 9 October?,"The test was endorsed for this week with no date. Source: my notes, 2 October.",make it a dated todo,leave it as a note,notes,70,72,68,66,78,exploit,Resolved true if a note by 2026-10-09 records the test and what it showed; false otherwise.,2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-058,cal-2026-10-02-s4,"Would one day a week with no new crewmate tasks, only reviews, raise what I learn from the fleet?","Two agent-free days stayed an intention. Source: my notes, 2 October.",make one review-only day a week,keep launching daily,notes,66,64,78,72,74,explore,Resolved by a later note comparing a review-only week with a normal one; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-059,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would working the one-loop QED beta function by hand again teach me more than an interactive QED lab would?,"My QED note derives it in four lines from one integral. Source: my notes, 24 September.",redo it by hand before using a lab,learn the rest from the lab,notes,68,56,90,70,72,explore,"Resolved by a later note judging either: true if the hand derivation is credited with something the lab did not show; unresolved otherwise.",2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-060,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Is the Open questions page listing todos I no longer intend to do?,"Two of its todos are now crewmate tasks; one was parked. Source: Open questions page.",prune it in a closing note this week,leave it as it is,notes,66,70,66,70,78,exploit,"Resolved by a closing note by 2026-10-09: true if it drops or parks at least one item still tagged todo.",2026-10-09,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-061,cal-2026-10-02-s4,"Would resolution rules that each name a concrete file, page or API let more cards resolve automatically?","Only 21 of 305 questions could be resolved so far. Source: raw.toon.",require every rule to name an artefact,allow note-based rules,calibration,74,62,78,58,80,exploit,"Resolved at the next resolution pass: true if cards with artefact-named rules resolve at a higher rate than note-based ones.",session 5,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-062,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would turning each effective variable into a card in session 5 test it faster than waiting for resolutions?,"Three candidate effective variables sit in notes. Source: my notes.",put each effective variable on a card in session 5,wait for ten resolutions each,calibration,74,58,80,60,78,exploit,Resolved by a later note judging an effective variable from cards rather than resolutions; unresolved otherwise.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-063,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would a weekly hour without screens produce first-hand observations more often than an hour with my visuals?,"First-hand observations are due three days a week. Source: my notes, 2 October.",schedule a screen-free hour for observations,draw observations from my visuals,notes,66,60,86,64,72,explore,Resolved by a later note comparing the sources of October's first-hand notes; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-064,cal-2026-10-02-s4,"Would I answer a re-asked card differently with no new evidence, a week later?","No card has yet been re-asked unchanged. Source: raw.toon.",re-ask five old cards unchanged in each session,re-ask only when evidence changes,calibration,72,56,82,62,76,explore,"Resolved from session 5 if it re-asks five session-4 cards unchanged: true if two or more move by 20 points or more.",session 5,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-065,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would a weekly one-line status note do everything a status feed would?,"A separate status feed was endorsed. Source: my notes, 2 October.",write a weekly status note instead,build the feed,notes,64,62,72,74,72,exploit,"Resolved by whichever lands first: true if a weekly status note appears and no feed is briefed by 2026-10-31.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-066,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would a hardware security key on GitHub cut my risk of a hard-to-undo failure more than the token audit?,"My expected failure is a leaked credential, a mass deletion or a bad deploy. Source: my notes.",add a hardware key first,finish the token audit first,synthesis,66,62,78,66,72,explore,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note on a failure names the missing safeguard; then resolved by it.,2027-01-02,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-067,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would one weekly block on Shimura varieties keep that thread alive through the étale month?,"The étale month is meant to be on one field alone. Source: my notes, 2 October.",keep a weekly Shimura block,pause Shimura varieties until December,notes,64,62,76,66,76,explore,"Resolved by a note in December: true if a Shimura-variety note is dated in November; false otherwise.",2026-12-01,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-068,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would a month on quantum field theory after the étale month produce more than a second mathematics month?,"Physics notes run alongside the mathematics ones. Source: my notes, 24 September.",plan December for quantum field theory,plan December for mathematics,notes,66,60,88,62,70,explore,Resolved by a later note naming December's focus and judging it; unresolved otherwise.,2027-01-05,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-069,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would a cheaper model record a Calibrator session as faithfully as the current one?,"Recording is mostly mechanical: append, restore and resolve. Source: raw.toon history.",use a cheaper model for the append step,keep the current model for recordings,project,68,62,74,66,72,explore,Resolved by a later note comparing a cheaper model's recording with the current one; unresolved otherwise.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-070,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would a pre-push secret hook in every crewmate worktree catch something GitHub's push protection misses?,"Push protection covers known token formats, not private paths. Source: my notes, 2 October.",add the hook to every worktree,rely on push protection,synthesis,68,64,74,62,74,exploit,Resolved true if a note by 2026-12-31 records the hook blocking a push that push protection allowed; unresolved otherwise.,2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-071,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Is Calibrator the most useful thing I built this month?,"Three sessions, 305 answered cards and 26 notes on 2 October. Source: raw.toon.",point the next tooling effort at Calibrator,point it elsewhere,synthesis,64,60,76,66,76,exploit,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note ranks this month's builds; then resolved by it.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-072,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Is the next structural tool more useful to students than to practising engineers?,"I know no practising engineer; a lecturer is the next contact. Source: my notes, 2 October.",aim the next tool at students,aim it at practising engineers,synthesis,66,62,74,64,74,explore,"Resolved by the first outside feedback on a structural tool: true if it comes from a student or teacher.",2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-073,cal-2026-10-02-s4,"Will the bandit visual's hours mode, if built, be used in its first week?","An hours-allocation input mode was endorsed before I would use it. Source: my notes, 2 October.",build the hours mode,drop the bandit for allocating hours,notes,64,60,68,76,70,exploit,Resolved true if a note within seven days of the mode shipping records an allocation made with it; false if none.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-074,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would a listener for étale cohomology be easier to find online than in person?,"One listener is planned for November. Source: my notes, 2 October.",look for one in an online study group,look for one person I know,notes,64,60,78,62,74,explore,"Resolved by the note recording the November explanation: true if the listener was found online.",2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-075,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would I finish more than five todos in October if my bet list held eight?,"My five todos are chosen through cards each session. Source: my notes, 2 October.",raise the list to eight,keep it at five,calibration,62,64,70,66,74,exploit,"Resolved by a note on 2026-10-31 counting October's completed todos: true if more than five.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-076,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Will I write at least five mental-computation notes in October?,"#mental-computation was my most used tag in September. Source: my notes.",keep ladders as my main mathematics practice,use the blocks for textbook problems,notes,64,62,66,66,78,exploit,"Resolved by counting notes tagged mental-computation dated 2026-10-01 to 2026-10-31: true if five or more.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-077,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would posting the Calibrator blog post outside my site get one reply I learn from?,"No outside reader is known to use the site. Source: my notes.",post it in one outside forum,keep it on the site only,notes,64,58,78,66,70,explore,Resolved true if a note by 2026-11-30 records a reply to the post from outside the site; false if posted with none.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-078,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Will I open the motives-and-periods visual in the first week of the étale month?,"It is live since 2 October; November is for étale cohomology. Source: site PR 126.",open the étale month with the visual,open it with a computation,project,66,60,74,58,76,explore,Resolved true if a note dated 2026-11-01 to 2026-11-07 uses or links the visual; false otherwise.,2026-11-07,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-079,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would firstmate's recording template be a better home for the resolution pass than each brief?,"Each recording brief names the resolution pass by hand. Source: raw.toon history.",add the pass to firstmate's recording template,keep naming it in each brief,project,64,70,68,52,78,exploit,Resolved true if firstmate's recording template includes a resolution pass by 2026-10-31; false otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-080,cal-2026-10-02-s4,"Would tagging September's agent-written notes, not only new ones, change which notes I trust?","Agents wrote most of September's notes; no tag marks them. Source: my notes, 2 October.",tag September's notes as well,tag new notes only,notes,64,58,72,64,72,exploit,"Resolved by a later note after the tag lands: true if it names a note I now trust less.",2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-081,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would a status feed I would actually read be generated from commit messages?,"Commits already describe what landed each day. Source: GitHub.",generate the feed from commits,write the feed by hand,project,66,62,74,56,72,explore,"Resolved by the shipped feed: true if it is generated from commits and a later note says I read it.",2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-082,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Did I open any one visualisation on at least three days this week?,"None of the 56 is ranked by my own use. Source: visualisations catalogue.",put it at the top of the catalogue,leave the order as it is,project,62,54,74,66,70,exploit,Resolved by my answer as a fact about this week; a later note may name the visual.,next session,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-083,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would the information-cohomology afternoon fit inside one of the two weekly mathematics blocks?,"Both are planned for October. Source: my notes, 2 October.",spend the first block on it,book a separate afternoon,notes,62,66,64,54,80,exploit,Resolved true if the note recording the information-cohomology afternoon is also a mathematics-block note; false otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-084,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would an agent from another model family find more errors in a mental-computation ladder than the fleet's own model?,"One agent check of a ladder is due by 31 October. Source: my notes, 2 October.",use another model family for the check,use the fleet's model,notes,62,54,78,60,72,explore,Resolved by a later note comparing both models on one ladder; unresolved otherwise.,2026-11-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-085,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Is the status feed worth a crewmate this month rather than after the token audit?,"A status feed separate from notes was endorsed. Source: my notes, 2 October.",brief the status feed this month,brief it after the audit lands,project,64,66,64,56,74,exploit,"Resolved by the date of the status-feed brief: true if before the token audit's note.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-086,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Is the item I most want to keep on the Open questions page one I have not touched in a month?,"Todos live there alongside open questions. Source: Open questions page.",date it or drop it this week,leave it untouched,notes,58,58,72,70,66,exploit,Resolved by my answer in session 5; unresolved otherwise.,session 5,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-087,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would a first-time visitor be better served by a home page that leads with the notes rather than the visuals?,"The catalogue has 56 visualisations; notes are one long page. Source: visualisations catalogue.",lead the home page with the notes,lead it with the visuals,project,60,58,76,64,66,explore,Unresolvable automatically unless a later note reports a visitor's reaction to either.,2026-12-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-088,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would one lecture series on quantum field theory beat my notes-and-labs approach to physics?,"My physics is notes and interactive labs. Source: my notes, 24 September.",follow one lecture series in December,keep notes and labs,notes,60,54,86,62,64,explore,Resolved by a later note judging a lecture series against my notes; unresolved otherwise.,2027-01-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-089,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Will beamdiag gain no new features through 31 October?,"New features are on the stop list until an engineer has used it. Source: my notes, 2 October.",keep beamdiag features on the stop list,take them off the list,notes,62,60,60,58,76,exploit,Resolved true if yujieteo/beamdiag gains no feat commit from 2026-10-03 to 2026-10-31; false otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-090,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Will a Calibrator podcast episode be one I listen to in full?,"One episode from my Calibrator notes was endorsed for this month. Source: my notes, 2 October.",make the episode this month,drop the episode,notes,58,56,70,64,66,exploit,"Resolved by a later note on the episode: true if it says I listened to it in full.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-091,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would a call counter on my WebMCP tools record a non-test call before 30 June 2027?,"The tools record nothing; a counter was endorsed. Source: my notes, 2 October.",add the counter now,add it when a browser ships WebMCP,notes,60,58,66,62,66,exploit,Resolved true if a counter records a non-test call by 2027-06-30; false if one runs with none; unresolved without a counter.,2027-06-30,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-092,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Will at least three people I know join an FPL mini-league I start before 10 October?,"A mini-league with people I know is a dated todo. Source: my notes, 2 October.",start my own league,join an existing league with one friend,notes,58,60,66,58,70,exploit,"Resolved by the note naming the league: true if I started it and three or more people I know joined by 2026-10-10.",2026-10-10,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-093,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Will I read this session's digest note before answering session 5?,"Session 3's notes now open with a five-point digest. Source: my notes, 2 October.",keep a digest above each session's notes,drop the digest,calibration,62,54,70,50,76,exploit,Resolved by my answer in session 5; unresolved otherwise.,session 5,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-094,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Would a post on the ten swapped cards be more useful to a reader than a summary of the whole session?,"The swapped cards split five and five between actions and propositions. Source: my notes.",write the post about the swapped cards,summarise the session,notes,60,54,76,52,68,explore,"Resolved by the published post: true if its subject is the swapped cards.",2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-095,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Will I leave certificates untouched through 31 October?,"Certificates are on my stop-doing list. Source: my notes, 2 October.",keep certificates on the stop list,take them off the list,notes,60,58,62,56,72,exploit,Resolved true if no note dated by 2026-10-31 records enrolment or work on a certificate; false otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-096,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Will I leave the four learning projects untouched through 31 October?,"A full-stack app, a DevOps container, a compiler and an automation project. Source: my notes.",keep them on the stop list,take them off the list,notes,60,58,62,56,72,exploit,Resolved true if no yujieteo repository or note by 2026-10-31 records work on any of the four; false otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-097,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Will the site's playbooks still call the dedicated E2E repository pending on 31 October?,"The plan for that repository was dropped. Source: SKILLS.md.",brief a crewmate to update the playbooks now,leave them until a port needs it,project,58,60,62,54,70,exploit,Resolved true if SKILLS.md or skills/verify.md still calls the E2E repository pending on 2026-10-31.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-098,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Will I leave Kontsevich's formality theorem unstated through 31 October?,"A precise statement is on my stop-doing list. Source: my notes, 2 October.",keep it on the stop list,take it off the list,notes,56,54,60,54,70,exploit,Resolved true if no note dated by 2026-10-31 states the formality theorem precisely; false otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-099,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Will I leave the cerebral-folate literature search untouched through 31 October?,"It is on my stop-doing list. Source: my notes, 2 October.",keep it on the stop list,take it off the list,notes,56,54,60,52,66,exploit,Resolved true if no note dated by 2026-10-31 summarises evidence on cerebral folate deficiency; false otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
  cal-20261002-s4-100,cal-2026-10-02-s4,Will option pricing stay in its one parking note through 31 October?,"Option pricing is parked rather than dropped. Source: my notes, 2 October.",keep it parked,unpark it with a date,notes,54,50,58,50,64,exploit,Resolved true if no #finance note other than FPL is dated 2026-10-03 to 2026-10-31; false otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-02T07:45:00Z"
